  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "While probing the Flower Wine Monk inheritance, Fang Yuan uses Earth Communication Ear Grass and hears a buzzing like a chainsaw from the centipede nest.",
        "chapters": [
          129
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_flower_wine_monk",
          "char_fang_yuan",
          "gu_earth_communication_ear_grass"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "At rank three he draws it out with leaked aura, seizes it when it coils around his waist, and uses Spring Autumn Cicada’s aura to force it to surrender, then refines away its wild consciousness in a few breaths. After that it coils around his arm under his will.",
        "chapters": [
          162
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "capture",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_spring_autumn_cicada"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Living Steel Gu is its healing Gu worm. After about an hour of black smoky steel essence, the razors grow back shiny and most injuries on its dark gold exoskeleton heal. Without that Gu, the razors would take at least half a year to fully grow back. It uses little primeval essence and has strong attack power, but is weak at healing itself.",
        "chapters": [
          177
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "healing-the-razors",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_healing_gu"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
